# Page debug flags

## Debug button

- Every page that needs dev-only controls gets a **Debug** button (bottom-right), same pattern as Search / Library (`fixed bottom-4 right-4`, slide-over panel, `BugIcon`).
- The panel and its toggles render **only when `import.meta.env.DEV`**. Production always uses the current shipped defaults.
- Keep flags compact (small segmented toggles). Put hints in `title` tooltips, not large cards.
- Colocate page flags in that page’s debug panel (or a `*DebugPanel` component used only there). Do not dump unrelated flags into other pages.

## Dev design pages (`app/dev-pages`)

Temp design / comparison pages are **auto-discovered** — no edits to `routes.ts` or a shared registry.

- **Add:** create `app/dev-pages/<unique-slug>.tsx` (kebab-case slug; pick a name that will not collide with other agents’ pages).
- **Export:** `export const devPage = { label: "Short nav label" }` plus a default page component. URL becomes `/dev/<slug>`. Nav links appear bottom-right (above the Debug button), DEV only.
- **Iterate in place:** when asked to change a design on an existing dev page, or make new variants from a specific design on that page, **replace that same file’s contents**. Do **not** create another dev page. Drop the previous exploration UI unless the user asks to keep it.
- **Delete:** remove that file only. Do not touch `routes.ts`, `DebugPagesNav`, or other pages.
- **Authoring:** keep **all newly generated UI in that one file** (variants, mocks, helpers). Do **not** split into `app/components/...` during exploration. **Reuse existing app components** when they already fit.
- **Ship a winner:** implement on the real page(s), extract into proper component files as needed, then **delete** the `app/dev-pages/<slug>.tsx` file.

## When changing UI

When asked to change UI (layout, chrome, colors, components, etc.):

1. **Default: preserve the current UI** behind a **dev-only feature flag** in **that page’s** Debug panel.
2. Ship the new UI as the default; the flag switches back to the previous version for comparison.
3. Name flags clearly (e.g. Card: Glass / Legacy, Progress: Cover / Original).
4. Wire production paths so they **always** take the new default — never the legacy branch — unless `import.meta.env.DEV` and the flag says otherwise.

## Opt out of preserving

If the user says **not** to save / keep / preserve the current UI (e.g. “don’t keep the old one”, “no feature flag”, “replace it”):

- **Do not** add a legacy/flag path.
- **Notify the user** in the reply that the previous UI was discarded and is not recoverable via Debug.

## Do not

- Leave temp design-comparison pages around after a winner is chosen (see apple-glass design exploration rule).
- Expose these UI rollback flags outside DEV.
- Edit a shared registry / `routes.ts` to add or remove a dev page.
- Split exploration UI into extra component files before a winner is chosen.
- Spawn a new `app/dev-pages/*.tsx` when iterating on an existing one (replace in place instead).
